Backport of moment PR #6015 (commit 9a3b5894f3d5d602948ac8a02e4ee528a49ca3a3)
for CVE-2022-31129: ReDoS in preprocessRFC2822.

The comment-stripping regex used a negated class /\([^)]*\)/ that allowed a
nested/unbalanced run of '(' characters to trigger quadratic-time backtracking.
Tightening the class to [^()]* stops the inner match at any bracket, removing
the catastrophic backtracking while preserving RFC 2822 comment stripping.

Both the ES module source (src/lib/create/from-string.js) and the shipped
UMD build (moment.js, the package "main") are updated so the fix is present
regardless of which entry point is loaded.

--- a/src/lib/create/from-string.js
+++ b/src/lib/create/from-string.js
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@ function untruncateYear(yearStr) {
 function preprocessRFC2822(s) {
     // Remove comments and folding whitespace and replace multiple-spaces with a single space
     return s
-        .replace(/\([^)]*\)|[\n\t]/g, ' ')
+        .replace(/\([^()]*\)|[\n\t]/g, ' ')
         .replace(/(\s\s+)/g, ' ')
         .replace(/^\s\s*/, '')
         .replace(/\s\s*$/, '');
--- a/moment.js
